        "name": "SVD-Based Hankel Minimal Realization",
        "pseudocode": "Input: amplitude function f, depth D\nOutput: minimal realization (T, alpha, omega, dim)\n\n1. Build Hankel matrix H[u,v] = f(u ++ v) for |u|,|v| <= D\n2. SVD: H = U Sigma V*\n3. Rank r = #{sigma_i > tol}\n4. U_r = U[:,:r] * sqrt(Sigma_r), V_r = sqrt(Sigma_r) * V*[:r,:]\n5. alpha = V_r[:,0], omega = U_r[0,:]\n6. For each g: build H_g[u,v] = f(u++g++v), T_g = U_r^+ H_g V_r^+\n7. Return (T, alpha, omega, r)",
